1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Bc5 {[A bit of a surprise. I think I had always
assumed that this was no good because of 4 Nxe5, but now I realized that Black
can reply Qg5. So I castled, making Nxe5 a real threat]} 4. O-O Nd4 {[Another
surprise, showing me that 4.c3 would have been much better.]} 5. Nxd4 Bxd4 6.
c3 Bb6 7. d4 c6 {[Surprising me once again, I think I was under the impression
that he would have to play e5xd4]} 8. Ba4 d6 {[By now I must have decided that
my brain was not working properly that day, so I agreed to a draw, either at
his suggestion or by playing for a draw myself by dxe5 and the exchange of
queens, I can't remember which. Notes by Oliver Penrose, from memory, on 8
Sept 2004!} 1/2-1/2

